    "# BME 603/606: Computational Methods for Biological Modeling & Simulation\n",
    "## In-Class Activity: Boolean Network Models\n",
    "\n",
    "Today's topic: **Boolean Networks**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Synchronous Updates** — implement a 3-node network and track how states evolve over time.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Attractors and Basins** — map the entire state space, find fixed points and limit cycles, and determine the basin of attraction for each.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Asynchronous Updates** — implement a stochastic update scheme and see how it changes the system's dynamics.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Challenge (Bonus)** — build a Boolean model of the MAPK/ERK signaling cascade with negative feedback and observe oscillations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's get started!"
   ]
