    "---\n",
    "## Part 1: Synchronous Updates\n",
    "\n",
    "### Background: Boolean States\n",
    "\n",
    "In systems biology, we often model the state of a gene or protein using a Boolean variable:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **1 (ON):** mRNA/protein is present above a threshold, kinase is phosphorylated, receptor is bound.\n",
    "- **0 (OFF):** Below detection threshold, dephosphorylated, unbound.\n",
    "\n",
    "A Boolean network with $n$ nodes has $2^n$ possible states. At each time step, every node is updated simultaneously based on the current state of its regulators.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The 3-Node Example\n",
    "\n",
    "Consider the following network:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$x_A(t+1) = x_B(t)$$\n",
    "$$x_B(t+1) = x_A(t) \\text{ AND } x_C(t)$$\n",
    "$$x_C(t+1) = \\text{NOT } x_A(t)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Biologically, this could represent:\n",
    "- A is activated by B.\n",
    "- B requires both A and C to be active.\n",
    "- C is repressed by A."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Exercise 1: Implement the Update Rule\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tasks:**\n",
