    "## Further Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "### Boolean Modeling in Cancer and Stem Cells\n",
    "\n",
    "Boolean networks have been used to model:\n",
    "- The mammalian cell cycle (see the 7-node model in lecture), where Rb, E2F, and cyclins form a bistable switch.\n",
    "- Cancer pathways, where knockouts (fixing a node to 0) alter the basin landscape and push cells toward uncontrolled proliferation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tools for Boolean Network Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "- **BooleNet:** A web-based Boolean network simulator with interactive attractor analysis.\n",
    "- **BioModelAnalyzer:** A tool for building and analyzing Boolean models of biological networks.\n",
